<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:04:16Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Watch live: Trump holds press conference after meeting with Xi, Putin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7e5e32a892467c274868c2a69c94fb0c7dec3141329126ea413cd4b8ebb37201</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T16:30:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261120-watch-live-trump-holds-press-conference-meeting-xi-putin--de6586fb5a55.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261120-watch-live-trump-holds-press-conference-meeting-xi-putin" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump is set to hold a White House press conference Friday, following his return to Washington after a four-day trip to Asia that saw him sit down for a first-ever trilateral meeting with Chinese President Xi Jinping and Russian President Vladimir Putin. Watch his conference live from 11:30am EST (5:30pm Paris time).</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Photography: A very French history</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9d46f143f3dfe4ae4148157ff624ffb8ae9c0070c0f61a36ee5b99db255281a3</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T16:28:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-photography-a-very-french-history--88d8d87c2e87.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-photography-a-very-french-history" /><summary type="html">From its use as creative expression to documenting our everyday reality, photography has become an essential and widely-accessible medium since its invention. Did you know, however, that the technology was developed in France? FRANCE 24's Tanishk Saha takes a look at the French legacy of photography.</summary></entry><entry><title>France investigates actor Depardieu, writer Houellebecq over alleged gang rape</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:463ec882333b72360262eb9203306414a8bba616df8ad08fa7fd5cb48c6d6313</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:16Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T16:27:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261120-france-investigates-gerard-depardieu-writer-houellebecq-over-alleged-gang-rape--a109fb153c3c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261120-france-investigates-gerard-depardieu-writer-houellebecq-over-alleged-gang-rape" /><summary type="html">French police are investigating allegations actor and convicted sex offender Gérard Depardieu raped and assaulted a woman with the complicity of bestselling author Michel Houellebecq during a 2018 film shoot, two sources following the case said Friday. The plaintiff has accused the film's director Guillaume Nicloux of being complicit in the abuse.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>'Blade Runner 2099' &amp; 'Rivals': The big TV shows to watch this month</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b0b21c5f23889a191847247a74a089879da947bf4f0887cebb8e2c90b2ec0e4d</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T16:17:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261120-blade-runner-2099-rivals-the-big-tv-shows-to-watch-this-month--fbe28f9d9ddb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261120-blade-runner-2099-rivals-the-big-tv-shows-to-watch-this-month" /><summary type="html">"Blade Runner" returns with a futuristic twist, while British bonkbuster "Rivals" is back with part two of season two. TV critic Dheepthika Laurent joins Eve Jackson to review the month’s big releases, including Netflix’s acclaimed Arctic comedy "North of North" and the lavish K-drama "Remarried Empress".</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>Gen Z protests spread across Europe: Mass rallies over cost of living in Spain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc4d4cd24be3212925e6d56a92a6f97c3c4e0bc16644b8108c2795fb8bdeab7a</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T15:41:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-gen-z-protests-spread-across-europe-mass-rallies-over-cost-of-living-in-spain--ddbdd241eaa4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-gen-z-protests-spread-across-europe-mass-rallies-over-cost-of-living-in-spain" /><summary type="html">Protesters across Europe are set took to the streets on Friday in a show of cross-border solidarity, joining coordinated demonstrations against the rising cost of living, militarisation and other causes, in a bid to increase pressure on their governments. Protesters across Europe are set to take to the streets on Friday in a show of cross-border solidarity, joining coordinated demonstrations against the rising cost of living, militarisation and other causes, in a bid to increase pressure on their governments. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid, Spain.</summary></entry><entry><title>French ex-PM Villepin announces presidential run</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:62e0ed7d380a39813f130a219149b6c0a48f3758f2ee96a14f936e41e73a4481</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T15:40:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-french-ex-pm-villepin-announces-presidential-run--ac78904c9c92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-french-ex-pm-villepin-announces-presidential-run" /><summary type="html">France's former prime minister and foreign minister Dominique de Villepin, famed abroad for his excoriating 2003 denunciation of US plans for invading Iraq, said on Friday he was running for president. Villepin enters an already crowded field of candidates seeking to succeed President Emmanuel Macron, with polls pointing towards a possible run-off between frontrunner Marine Le Pen of the far-right National Rally (RN) and hard-left France Unbowed (LFI) veteran Jean-Luc Melenchon.</summary></entry><entry><title>Shenzhen trilateral: Xi Jinping's 'masterclass in diplomatic theatre'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:06fd3fea2292d0b6b1f742222f2a6bbd72c23f94f766e2a049e3bac39faba22b</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:28Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T15:37:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261120-shenzhen-trilateral-xi-jinping-s-masterclass-in-diplomatic-theatre--3189c813d399.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261120-shenzhen-trilateral-xi-jinping-s-masterclass-in-diplomatic-theatre" /><summary type="html">Xi Jinping positioned himself as a great statesman when he met with the US president and Russia's Vladimir Putin for trilateral talks in Shenzhen this week. But while the Chinese president sparkled on the world stage, does he have anything to show for it? Seong-Hyon Lee, an associate at Harvard University Asia Center, tells us how the trilateral has come up short on deliverables.</summary><category term="Access Asia" /></entry><entry><title>Spain’s political crossroads, Europe’s wider stakes: Spaniards to vote in key election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:415bc663454374a0a824dd6add7bfe0c98fd649a9fa3782c0591f625c9488016</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T15:17:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261120-spains-political-crossroads-europes-wider-stakes-spaniards-to-vote-in-key-election--45b0fdce8813.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261120-spains-political-crossroads-europes-wider-stakes-spaniards-to-vote-in-key-election" /><summary type="html">The stakes are high – not only for people in Spain, but also for Europe. On November 29, the country holds a parliamentary election that could see the end of the Socialist-led government and potentially a coalition between the right and the far right, in one of the EU’s biggest and most influential member states. It could also signal the end of Pedro Sanchez’s third term in office. Among other things, the prime minister may pay the political price for two shocking train crashes and the migrant crisis in Spain’s North African exclave of Ceuta.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Jamaica's beaches are increasingly off limits to locals</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eea9c8e607a954e00271e317d7db324b334e8639b06bc80abe1877f7fe37d93e</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T14:55:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261120-jamaica-beaches-off-limits-to-locals-property-developers-hotels--8b1ba04df6ef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261120-jamaica-beaches-off-limits-to-locals-property-developers-hotels" /><summary type="html">Jamaica usually conjures up images of white sandy beaches, Rastafari culture and Bob Marley – but another reality exists. On this small Caribbean island, less than 1 percent of the coastline is freely accessible to local people. The rest has gradually been privatised, mostly for large hotel developments and private homes.</summary><category term="Reporters" /></entry><entry><title>Cincinnati Zoo's famed Fiona the hippo dies days after eating a visitor’s hat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf622a90e000eb417f5c38aba313e494085aee6c08efb73dc5fcf5ce67f013c6</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T14:48:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-cincinnati-zoo-s-famed-fiona-the-hippo-dies-days-after-eating-a-visitor-s-hat--855a27acfd5c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-cincinnati-zoo-s-famed-fiona-the-hippo-dies-days-after-eating-a-visitor-s-hat" /><summary type="html">Fiona, the hippo whose premature birth and fight for survival at the Cincinnati Zoo turned her into a global sensation nearly a decade ago, died Thursday from complications after swallowing a knit hat that was accidentally flung into her enclosure. She was 9 years old. “It is with extreme sadness that we share with you the devastating news that Fiona did not make it after multiple attempts from our amazing vets and keeper team to help her through what ended up being a medical emergency,” the zoo said in a statement.</summary></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: Burnham, Von der Leyen hail 'turning point' in EU-UK relations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:22139787a5bdbf1ec6f14db5be4b5c80e51dfb96a9befd34a93d30f538d12ba7</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T14:45:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-replay-burnham-von-der-leyen-hail-turning-point-in-eu-uk-relations--11760f4dc8e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-replay-burnham-von-der-leyen-hail-turning-point-in-eu-uk-relations" /><summary type="html">British Prime Minister Andy Burnham hailed a "landmark" deal with the European Union on Friday, as the two sides sealed pacts on food exports, emissions-trading schemes and youth mobility at a summit in Brussels. EU chief Ursula von der Leyen welcomed a "turning point" in ties with Britain following Brexit. Watch our replay.</summary></entry><entry><title>COP31 wrapping up in Turkey: Climate deal elusive as fossil fuels go unmentioned</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e0a2bee67da73686a0174dd09d84b21ce3bfa2abe1066cbe2e6c0bff276f3b1</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T14:38:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-cop31-wrapping-up-in-turkey-climate-deal-elusive-as-fossil-fuels-go-unmentioned--8b20e21a6d79.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-cop31-wrapping-up-in-turkey-climate-deal-elusive-as-fossil-fuels-go-unmentioned" /><summary type="html">The UN's COP31 climate talks were set to spill into overtime Friday as countries remained deadlocked over a draft deal that makes no mention of fossil fuels, with a host of other disputes also snarling negotiations. The talks come with a series of stark reminders of the urgency of climate action, from heatwaves in Europe and devastating floods in Nepal, while a record-breaking El Nino supercharges temperatures. FRANCE 24's Environment Editor Valerie Dekimpe tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Burnham hails 'landmark' EU-UK deal as 'good day' for Britain, Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c6f6708bf5372e9a84493aa1ee66671a35209707b893078134cf0fee0e1e2e1d</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T14:37:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-burnham-hails-landmark-eu-uk-deal-as-good-day-for-britain-europe--fb8ab97f4ef7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-burnham-hails-landmark-eu-uk-deal-as-good-day-for-britain-europe" /><summary type="html">Britain and the European Union agreed deals on trade, carbon emissions and youth movement on Friday, and pledged to rebuild ties with an “ambitious and dynamic” post-Brexit relationship. In a joint statement after a summit in Brussels, the UK and EU confirmed agreements that will scrap checks on the trade in plant and animal products, link their emissions trading schemes and let 100,000 young adults from each side live and work in the other's countries for up to three years. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Kethevane Gorjestani tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia pummels Ukraine with massive strikes, missile hits Poland</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:542a4c84a14fb205957faf60b0b159281aaea5515b3c2ee3ad3ec0121e66b9f5</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T14:36:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-russia-pummels-ukraine-with-massive-strikes-missile-hits-poland--ce7ff9895846.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-russia-pummels-ukraine-with-massive-strikes-missile-hits-poland" /><summary type="html">Moscow pounded Ukraine with massive strikes Friday, with Kyiv saying at least six people were killed in the capital, and neighbouring Poland reporting two Russian missiles likely landed in the south-east corner of the NATO country, accusing Moscow of a "provocation." Hours earlier, Russia's Vladimir Putin vowed a "painful" response to Kyiv's strikes on Moscow's Crimea bridge after holding a summit with China's Xi Jinping and US President Donald Trump. FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg reports from Kyiv, Ukraine.</summary></entry><entry><title>'GTA VI': When the biggest-ever entertainment release becomes the biggest headline</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aaeff9a7454979a14a46f6752dfa778e9ba7a0501b16d7a19de520f95704010f</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T14:35:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/scoop/20261120-gta-vi-when-the-biggest-ever-entertainment-release-becomes-the-biggest-headline--4050c1afc6b0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/scoop/20261120-gta-vi-when-the-biggest-ever-entertainment-release-becomes-the-biggest-headline" /><summary type="html">This week FRANCE 24's media show "Scoop" looks at how the press covered the release of "Grand Theft Auto VI". Pre-orders and first-day sales totalled more than $2.3 billion. What does the game and the franchise's success mean for the future of entertainment? Our guest is Margaret Wallace, a video game developer and an associate professor of the practice of media innovation at Boston University.</summary><category term="Scoop" /></entry><entry><title>France probes suspected leak of confidential information to Le Pen's party</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7272b1a1f65d509060ae7d9047eb570d79eba3f30acf147be60f915a8ab1678b</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:55Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T14:35:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261120-france-probes-suspected-leak-confidential-information-le-pen-far-right-party--afb5e4d00407.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261120-france-probes-suspected-leak-confidential-information-le-pen-far-right-party" /><summary type="html">French authorities are investigating whether a former senior official at the Interior Ministry leaked confidential information about judicial investigations into far-right leader Marine Le Pen's National Rally, adding to the party's legal woes ahead of a presidential election next year in which Le Pen is the current frontrunner.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>A decade after Brexit, do Britons regret leaving the EU?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4e3ff65591f3e097aa1f1c1ce228e5901713e100362f8c35eb3357f1dc327c8d</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T14:34:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-a-decade-after-brexit-do-britons-regret-leaving-the-eu--5a9915065abb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-a-decade-after-brexit-do-britons-regret-leaving-the-eu" /><summary type="html">Britain and the European Union went through a bitter divorce, then slowly began trying to rebuild their relationship. UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham met the EU's top officials in Brussels on Friday for a summit he has described as a step towards undoing a decade of damage caused by the 2016 vote to leave the bloc. But how do the British public feel about closer ties with the EU – and, potentially, rejoining it?</summary></entry><entry><title>Does staggered consent actually protect young people?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b207c753bfe9fb1656de85a0f4f84f0aa5ed6af0e8ca7e0738d8ca43c9812c69</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:04:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T14:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261120-does-staggered-consent-actually-protect-young-people--b74fdbb9cde1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261120-does-staggered-consent-actually-protect-young-people" /><summary type="html">Following recent scandals involving two iconic British comedians, the UK government is considering the introduction of staggered age consent. Annette Young talks to Katherine Allen from the Institute of Social Justice and Crime in the UK about whether such laws work. Also the social costs of femicide; how do loved ones cope with such a loss, and what support is available to families in the wake of such a tragedy? Plus we meet the women who are challenging the traditions of Mexican mariachi music, a world that remains largely male dominated.</summary><category term="The 51%" /></entry><entry><title>El Salvador: Nayib Bukele, self-proclaimed “coolest dictator on earth”, is seeking a third term</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe2bd0a0a2b4c73eb27c48da38f29e761b57f822e32e5347dc5ab7ad612f7100</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:04:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T12:07:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/el-salvador-nayib-bukele-self-proclaimed-coolest-dictator-on-earth-is-seeking-a-third-term--1aebd0b55990.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/el-salvador-nayib-bukele-self-proclaimed-coolest-dictator-on-earth-is-seeking-a-third-term" /><summary type="html">🇸🇻 El Salvador’s President Nayib Bukele, who calls himself the “coolest dictator on earth”, is seeking a third term after changing the Constitution to scrap presidential term limits. His war on gangs has made him hugely popular, but also sparked serious human rights concerns.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴 France seeks UN Security Council meeting after Russian strikes hit European embassies in Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5f5ab382cead5bc9abc526af9e408c561f96ae88723a0034cadc9960cec5cd13</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T12:04:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-live-deadly-russian-attacks-damage-two-bridges-in-kyiv-mayor-says--388c1dca5fe6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-live-deadly-russian-attacks-damage-two-bridges-in-kyiv-mayor-says" /></entry><entry><title>Malaysia's unwanted refugees: The plight of the Rohingya</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f57e41711375af0c00723502debcb6ce21cabc2e07e1bc7c711cf43dfa3bc824</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:04:07Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T11:28:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261120-malaysia-s-unwanted-refugees-the-plight-of-the-rohingya--4971af38a2e1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261120-malaysia-s-unwanted-refugees-the-plight-of-the-rohingya" /><summary type="html">On November 19, the International Court of Justice delivered a historic ruling: finding Myanmar guilty of committing genocide against the Rohingya in 2017. Malaysia has long been a supporter of the persecuted Muslim minority. But its role as a safe haven is coming to an end, amid a rise in hate speech and calls for the expulsion of Rohingya via social media.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Italy strike draws workers, students into nationwide protests over wages and living costs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f091ea94b025d1e22acee04c531c1aedc48a4c47c11f8a378202cd7a51862ebc</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:04:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T11:25:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-italy-strike-draws-workers-students-into-nationwide-protests-over-wages-and-living-costs--1ef6833dc816.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-italy-strike-draws-workers-students-into-nationwide-protests-over-wages-and-living-costs" /><summary type="html">A nationwide strike was expected to disrupt schools, hospitals and local transport across Italy on Friday as workers and students began marching in dozens of cities to demand higher wages, lower living costs and greater social protections. The labor action coincided with an International Day of Student Mobilisation, with organisers planning demonstrations in more than 45 Italian cities. FRANCE 24's Seema Gupta reports from Rome, Italy.</summary></entry><entry><title>South Africa: High Court examines asylum seekers' detention at Lindela centre</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7798c202e71c52676cb11290322699c358bb5845f695bfe45e595ab378eca9b8</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:04:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T11:23:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-south-africa-high-court-examines-asylum-seekers-detention-at-lindela-centre--5cab48471759.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-south-africa-high-court-examines-asylum-seekers-detention-at-lindela-centre" /><summary type="html">South Africa's High Court judges visited the Lindela Repatriation Centre in Krugersdorp this week, ahead of delivering a ruling on 33 urgent applications concerning the detention of asylum seekers. The court is examining conflicting interpretations of a Constitutional Court ruling that prohibits the deportation of asylum seekers whose claims are still being processed. The case comes amid a wider and increasingly tense debate over immigration in South Africa, which has at times spilled over into deadly xenophobic violence. FRANCE 24's Eunice Masson reports from Cape Town, South Africa.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Our culture and identity': Deaf Nigerians embrace indigenous sign languages</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:52edecc963c0ddeafcb44ceee7e83d0186079d5996ca65b9cbfd053a23413084</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:04:16Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T11:21:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-our-culture-and-identity-deaf-nigerians-embrace-indigenous-sign-languages--88c07fe69111.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-our-culture-and-identity-deaf-nigerians-embrace-indigenous-sign-languages" /><summary type="html">With a quick flick of the wrist, Umaru Zayyanu conveys the phrase "I am a Nigerian". But the 37-year-old is not signing, rather in the west African nation's official sign language. Instead, he's using Hausa sign language. Such indigenous sign languages abound in Africa's most populous country, where deaf people were communicating with each other long before the advent of formal sign language taught in deaf schools, in 1960.</summary></entry></feed>
